+
+<!-- CARROT:SECTION:BEGIN BEHAVIOR -->
+### Behavior
+
+MAIN standby requests SET after each fresh gas press/release regardless of engagement/lateral activity. Inactive controls require a pedal cue and never execute a retry-blocked cue later. After brake/CANCEL in confirmed MAIN standby, a fresh press of at least 0.1s qualifies a release observation for at most 0.1s despite brief target blocking. Dashboard/wheel speeds, MAIN availability, units and drive gear must qualify at release and remain valid. Rearm only if the target and other current request conditions become valid within the original window; recovery never renews it. A new gas press, driver button, brake or invalid input clears the observation. MAIN tracking starts OFF independently of AutoEngage. Establish standby with the physical MAIN ON button after boot; gas release before MAIN activation cannot start cruise.
+<!-- CARROT:SECTION:END BEHAVIOR -->
+
+<!-- CARROT:SECTION:BEGIN USAGE -->
+### Usage
+
+While parked, update/restart with MAIN OFF, then press MAIN ON after boot to establish CRUISE standby. Retain the existing 0.5s MAIN settling and pedal/target conditions. If standby was already ON during restart, use a MAIN-OFF restart or actual stock ON from physical SET to synchronize.
+<!-- CARROT:SECTION:END USAGE -->
+
+<!-- CARROT:SECTION:BEGIN REFERENCE -->
+### Reference
+
+CarState, the button controller and Panda share initial MAIN OFF and physical MAIN transitions. This does not decode absolute OEM MAIN state; actual stock ON also synchronizes tracking. Automatic SET uses newly observed CLU11 samples, without 10ms delays or changing speed-matching timing memory. The new Panda profile requires dashboard 30–160km/h and each wheel 25–160km/h. Both wheels at least 30km/h retain the original admission; if either is below 30km/h, both must be within 5km/h of the dashboard. Recompute switch/counter parity for transmitted buttons and validate it in Panda. Observe actual ON for 0.5s; missing/interrupted feedback requires three seconds after the last transmission. Actual ON resets host/native consecutive attempts without shortening existing waits. Explicit MAIN OFF, brake, CANCEL, invalid inputs and existing pulse/retry bounds remain. Option OFF revokes transmission permission without clearing tracked MAIN state. Continue tracking physical MAIN changes while disabled; enabling alone cannot start cruise. Existing MAIN confirmation, fresh-pedal conditions and explicit MAIN-OFF blocking remain. Vehicle acceptance requires confirmation.
+<!-- CARROT:SECTION:END REFERENCE -->
